	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Usage

Start a coding agent on a task in its own Herdr tab via the `herd` keyword. Add `@agent`, `#repo`, `%space`, `=name` or `+wt` anywhere in the line, or paste a pull request link to review it on its own worktree.

![Starting a task](images/task.png)

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Start the agent.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open a form with every option.

Type `/` to pick one of your skills or slash commands.

![Picking a skill](images/skills.png)

Alternatively, select text anywhere and start a task with it via the Universal Action. Configure the Hotkey to open the form with the selected text as the task.

![The form](images/form.png)

See which agents need you via the `agents` keyword.

![Running agents](images/agents.png)

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Show the agent's tab in Herdr.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Write the agent a message.

Message a running agent via the `tell` keyword.

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Send the message.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⌥&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open a form showing the agent's recent output.

Remove worktrees whose pull request is merged or closed via the `tidy` keyword.

Change the keywords, default agent, repo folders and Space in the Workflow's Configuration. More settings and help: [github.com/sajansharmanz/herd-alfred-workflow](https://github.com/sajansharmanz/herd-alfred-workflow).

herd was written with the help of Claude Code, an AI coding tool.

Icon: [Sheep Icon Vectors by Vecteezy](https://www.vecteezy.com/free-vector/sheep-icon). Agent logos: [LobeHub Icons](https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons).
</string>
